  atem:
    line: Mara Okafor and the narrator plan to ask the parish council to delay mowing the orchard meadow strip until
      September to protect pollinators.
    focus: The text details the orchard's improved yield and the specific threat that early mowing poses to the
      wildflowers feeding essential insects.
    push: The author wants the reader to support the request to delay mowing because it protects the orchard's fruit
      production.
    pull: The text assumes the meadow strip is the orchard's primary pollinator source and that the council will
      accept the delay request.
